  "section_notes": "The final text keeps the 8-per-100,000 mandatory recall trigger with no transition, which directly exposes Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9), while the S2 ceiling of 7% (above 5% requiring corrective action) lets Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%) pass. Per-model results go to regulators and purchasers of that model but not to the general public, satisfying both red lines, and the 6-year retrofit deadline favours Northwind's low shut-off coverage. Reporting (24 hours) and suppression (36 months) are strong or acceptable on safety, and the 36-month suppression deadline sits at the HC-2 boundary."
